   8:     """
   9:     Cycle each solid odd-sided square to the next smaller centered square, wrapping a single pixel to a 9x9 square.
  10: 
  11:     Input structure:
  12:     - The grid has one dominant background color.
  13:     - Every foreground object is a separated 4-connected monochrome solid square.
  14:     - Square side lengths are odd and belong to the cycle 1, 3, 5, 7, 9.
  15: 
  16:     Rule:
  17:     - Clear the canvas to the background.
  18:     - Keep each square's color and center.
  19:     - Replace side length n by n - 2 when n > 1; replace side length 1 by side length 9.
  20: 
  21:     Key insight:
  22:     - The visible operation is on square size, not color: side lengths cycle 1 -> 9 -> 7 -> 5 -> 3 -> 1.
  23:     """
  24:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  25:     bg = get_bg(g)
  26:     components = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True, return_format="dict")
